## Mechanics — Vitest in Wen365

**Project layout** (enforced by `vitest.config.ts`):

- `test/unit/**/*.{test,spec}.ts` — node env, pure logic. Run via `pnpm test:unit`.
- `test/nuxt/**/*.{test,spec}.ts` — Nuxt env (auto-imports, components, composables). Run via `pnpm test:nuxt`.
- `test/factories/<domain>.ts` — domain-specific factories (when extracted; see §6).
- `test/nuxt/api/**` — API route tests with `setup()` + `$fetch()` (Tier 3 area; should grow).

Both run via `pnpm test`. Always run `pnpm type-check` and `pnpm lint` before claiming work done (per `AGENTS.md`).

**Async + time.**

```ts
beforeEach(() => {
  vi.useFakeTimers();
});

afterEach(() => {
  vi.useRealTimers();
});

it("retries with exponential backoff", async () => {
  const promise = serviceCall();

  await vi.runAllTimersAsync();

  await expect(promise).resolves.toEqual(expected);
});
```

Always restore real timers in `afterEach`. Never `await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, 1000))`.

**Mock isolation.**

```ts
beforeEach(() => {
  vi.clearAllMocks();
  // re-prime any default mock returns here
});
```

**Composable testing pattern (§2).** Mock at the process boundary — `$fetch` only. Let TanStack Query run.

```ts
const mockFetch = vi.fn();
global.$fetch = mockFetch as unknown as typeof global.$fetch;

it("does not fetch when address is null", async () => {
  const address = ref<string | null>(null);

  const { data } = usePortfolio(address);
  await flushPromises();

  expect(mockFetch).not.toHaveBeenCalled();
  expect(data.value).toBeUndefined();
});
```

**Component testing pattern (§4).** Stub external UI primitives to expose semantic attributes; render real DOM otherwise.

```ts
const uiStubs = {
  UCard: { template: '<div><slot name="header" /><slot /></div>' },
  UBadge: {
    inheritAttrs: false,
    props: ["color", "variant", "size"],
    template: '<span data-testid="badge" :data-color="color"><slot /></span>',
  },
};

async function mountCard(props: Record<string, unknown>) {
  return mountSuspended(NetWorthCard, { props, global: { stubs: uiStubs } });
}
```

**API route test pattern (Tier 3, §7).** Use `@nuxt/test-utils` to boot a test Nuxt instance and call routes via `$fetch`. Mock Alchemy / Supabase at the boundary; let Nitro, validation, error handlers, and the route itself run.

```ts
// test/nuxt/api/portfolio.test.ts
import { setup, $fetch } from "@nuxt/test-utils/e2e";
import { describe, it, expect } from "vitest";

await setup({ /* test fixture options */ });

describe("/api/portfolio/:address", () => {
  it("returns 401 when unauthenticated", async () => {
    await expect($fetch("/api/portfolio/0x0000000000000000000000000000000000000001"))
      .rejects.toMatchObject({ statusCode: 401 });
  });
});
```

**Commands.**

```bash
pnpm test          # all tests
pnpm test:unit     # node env only
pnpm test:nuxt     # Nuxt env only
pnpm test:watch    # watch mode
pnpm test:coverage # coverage report (diagnostic only — no targets, see §8)
```

